_birder"}, {"id": "mont_masq", "sprite": "festival_goer", "x": 52, "y": 29, "facing": "left", "move": "still", "trainer": "mont_masq"}, {"id": "mont_volc", "sprite": "astronomer", "x": 42, "y": 36, "facing": "down", "move": "still", "trainer": "mont_volc"}, {"id": "mont_fisher", "sprite": "fisher", "x": 31, "y": 11, "facing": "up", "move": "still", "trainer": "mont_fisher"}, {"id": "mont_trespass", "sprite": "explorer", "x": 26, "y": 35, "facing": "left", "move": "still", "trainer": "mont_trespass"}, {"id": "mont_jumbie", "sprite": "poet", "x": 27, "y": 35, "facing": "right", "move": "still", "trainer": "mont_jumbie"}, {"id": "montserrat_bureau", "sprite": "commuter", "x": 37, "y": 25, "facing": "down", "move": "still", "script": "montserrat_bureau", "name": "Bureau Clerk"}, {"id": "montserrat_homebound", "sprite": "sailor", "x": 37, "y": 26, "facing": "down", "move": "still", "script": "montserrat_homebound", "name": "Movements Clerk"}], "encounters": {"grass": [{"species": "cinderling", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 12}, {"species": "oriolet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 8, "time": ["dawn", "day", "dusk"]}, {"species": "duneskink", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 12, "weather": ["clear", "sunshine"]}, {"species": "kindlet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 12}, {"species": "flamingale", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 12, "weather": ["drizzle", "downpour"]}, {"species": "crumblet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 12}, {"species": "chipgull", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 10}, {"species": "flittermouse", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 10, "time": ["dusk", "night"]}, {"species": "jetling", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 8}, {"species": "croakle", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 8}, {"species": "swiftlet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 8, "time": ["dawn", "day", "dusk"]}, {"species": "soufrilla", "min": 97, "max": 99, "weight": 2, "weather": ["fog", "gale"]}], "water": [{"species": "dolphlet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 26}, {"species": "swelklet", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 22}, {"species": "pinchkin", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 18}, {"species": "plungebeak", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 14}, {"species": "baskling", "min": 95, "max": 97, "weight": 16}]}, "signs": [{"x": 39, "y": 27, "text": "LITTLE BAY, MONTSERRAT. The new capital, still building, with a black sand beach and a very nice view. The old capital is in the south and is buried."}, {"x": 28, "y": 32, "text": "EXCLUSION ZONE: SOUTH. No entry beyond the posted line, ever. The volcano does not read signs, and it is not interested in your reasons."}, {"x": 31, "y": 35, "text": "MONTSERRAT VOLCANO OBSERVATORY. Visitors welcome in the visitors' room. Please do not feed the seismograph."}, {"x": 25, "y": 34, "text": "PLYMOUTH, buried. The old capital lies under metres of ash and mud. What you can see of it are roofs."}, {"x": 32, "y": 21, "text": "THE EMERALD ISLE. Columbus named the island in 1493 for the Spanish abbey of Santa Maria de Montserrat. Irish Catholic settlers arrived in the 1630s and the island kept an Irish flavour: shamrocks, Irish surnames and place names like Kinsale and Cork Hill. It is called the Emerald Isle of the Caribbean.", "plaque": "mont_emerald", "title": "The Emerald Isle"}, {"x": 45, "y": 20, "text": "ST PATRICK'S DAY. Montserrat is one of the few places outside Ireland where 17 March is a public holiday. It marks the island's Irish roots and also a slave uprising planned for St Patrick's Day in 1768, which failed and is remembered as a day of freedom. The holiday is now a week-long festival of parades, music and masquerade.", "plaque": "mont_stpats", "title": "St Patrick's Day"}, {"x": 54, "y": 21, "text": "THE BADGE. Montserrat's coat of arms shows a woman in green with a golden harp and a cross, an image of Erin, Ireland personified. The island's flag carries the badge, and the Union Flag in the corner.", "plaque": "mont_badge", "title": "The Badge"}, {"x": 34, "y": 30, "text": "SOUFRIÈRE HILLS. After centuries of quiet, the volcano began to erupt on 18 July 1995 and has been active in phases since. A lava dome grows, collapses and sends ash and fast, hot pyroclastic flows down the valleys. The south of the island is now an Exclusion Zone.", "plaque": "mont_volcano", "title": "Soufrière Hills"}, {"x": 26, "y": 33, "text": "PLYMOUTH. Plymouth, Montserrat's old capital, was evacuated in 1995 and buried by repeated ash and mud flows from 1997. Roofs and clock faces poke out of the grey like a Caribbean Pompeii. It can only be seen from a safe distance.", "plaque": "mont_plymouth", "title": "Plymouth"}, {"x": 43, "y": 36, "text": "25 JUNE 1997. A series of pyroclastic flows swept down the valleys on the east side of the volcano and killed nineteen people who had gone into the zone to look after their farms. It was the worst day of the eruption and the reason for strict, enforced zones.", "plaque": "mont_1997", "title": "25 June 1997"}, {"x": 32, "y": 35, "text": "THE OBSERVATORY. A small team of scientists at the Montserrat Volcano Observatory watches the volcano around the clock with seismographs, GPS, cameras and gas sensors. They set the hazard level, and the island plans its life around it.", "plaque": "mont_observatory", "title": "The Observatory"}, {"x": 51, "y": 19, "text": "AIR STUDIOS. The Beatles' producer George Martin built a recording studio on Montserrat in 1979. For ten years big acts came to record in the sun, including Dire Straits' Brothers in Arms and The Police's Synchronicity. Hurricane Hugo wrecked it in 1989 and it never reopened.", "plaque": "mont_air", "title": "AIR Studios"}, {"x": 61, "y": 22, "text": "THE MONTSERRAT ORIOLE. Black and bright yellow, the national bird, and found nowhere else on Earth. The eruption destroyed much of its forest and numbers crashed. It now lives in the Centre Hills, where a nature reserve protects it.", "plaque": "mont_oriole", "title": "The Montserrat Oriole"}, {"x": 34, "y": 12, "text": "BLACK SAND. Montserrat's beaches are dark grey and black, from ground-down volcanic rock, and by noon are hot enough to make you hop. The old pale beaches in the south are buried.", "plaque": "mont_black_sand", "title": "Black Sand"}, {"x": 28, "y": 30, "text": "GARIBALDI HILL. A viewpoint on the edge of the Exclusion Zone, from which you can look across the ash to buried Plymouth and the plume of the volcano. It is, as every visitor says, a good place to think about things.", "plaque": "mont_garibaldi", "title": "Garibaldi Hill"}, {"x": 50, "y": 22, "text": "GOAT WATER. Goat water is Montserrat's national dish: a spicy goat stew with cloves, thyme and hot pepper, eaten with a bread roll. It is called water because it is more of a broth, and goat because it is.", "plaque": "mont_goat_water", "title": "Goat Water"}, {"x": 58, "y": 24, "text": "THE AIRPORT. W.H. Bramble Airport was wrecked by the eruption in 1997 and, for a while, the island was cut off, with only a ferry and helicopters. A new airport at Gerald's opened in 2005, and small planes now bring visitors in from Antigua.", "plaque": "mont_airport", "title": "The Airport"}], "legend_extra": {"_water": {"deep": "#0a4a6e", "deep_top": "#2a90a8", "shallow": "#3fb8b0"}, "$": {"tile": "sea", "colour": "#126f8a"}, "~": {"tile": "water", "colour": "#2c9cae"}, "w": {"tile": "shallow", "colour": "#6fd0c0"}, ".": {"tile": "grass", "colour": "#4e9a3a"}, ",": {"tile": "tall_grass", "colour": "#3f8a34", "prop": "short"}, "s": {"tile": "sand", "colour": "#5a5755"}, "p": {"tile": "sand", "colour": "#464442"}, "a": {"tile": "sand", "colour": "#85807b"}, "A": {"tile": "sand", "colour": "#6e6a66"}, "t": {"tile": "tree_oak", "prop": "palm"}, "e": {"tile": "tree_oak", "prop": "palm"}, "h": {"tile": "tree_pine", "colour": "#2f6a30"}, "r": {"tile": "rock", "colour": "#6f6a64"}, "d": {"tile": "rock", "colour": "#4a4644", "prop": "gritstone"}, "#": {"tile": "path", "colour": "#cdbf9d"}, "=": {"tile": "road", "colour": "#aaa294"}, ":": {"tile": "cobbles", "colour"